course: dictionary
lesson: 5636
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Context, the words and sentences around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The tall bows of the great liner taking shape overhead through the fog» is about a ship, because bows are the front of a boat and a fog hangs over the sea.
explain: Ask: what word would fit here? If the sentence is about the sea, the word probably means a ship. If it is about a bin, it probably means a bag. Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Liner also has some surprising meanings. A bin liner is a bag that sits inside a rubbish bin, and eyeliner is make-up drawn along the eyelids. Each one fits its own situation. If you are not sure, look at the other words in the sentence.
fact: A liner is a big passenger ship that sails across oceans on regular routes.
fact: «Ocean liner» and «cruise liner» are phrases for big passenger ships.
fact: A liner is also something put inside another thing to line or protect it, such as a bin liner (a bin bag in the UK) or a nappy liner.
fact: Eyeliner is make-up drawn along the eyelids.
fact: In baseball and cricket, a line drive is a ball hit hard and low.
exercise: «The tall bows of the great liner taking shape overhead through the fog» What is the liner here? | Make-up for the eyelids | A ball hit hard and low | *A big passenger ship | A bin bag
exercise: Mum says, «Put a new liner in the kitchen bin.» What is a liner here? | *A bin bag | A big ship on the ocean | A cricket ball | Make-up for the eyes
exercise: Mia put on eyeliner before the party. What is eyeliner? | A ship that sails across oceans | A bag for rubbish | A ball hit hard and low | *Make-up drawn along the eyelids
test: «The ocean liner sailed across the Atlantic with hundreds of passengers on board.» What kind of liner is this? | *A big passenger ship | A ball hit hard and low | A pen with a thin tip | A bag for rubbish
test: The batter hit a line drive over the infield. What is a line drive? | *A ball hit hard and low | Make-up drawn along the eyelids | A big ship on the sea | A bag that lines a bin
exam: The players cheered when the ball flew low past the fielders, a line drive hit hard and low, while the crowd remembered the old liner that once crossed the ocean. What does liner mean in the second part? | A bin bag | Eyeliner | *A big passenger ship | A line drive
